{"name":"Sanctuary","hex":"#d4c9a6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sanctuary","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place of safety, refuge, or protection.","An area set aside for protection."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sanctuary"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sanctuary","blocks":[{"text":"A sanctuary, in its original meaning, is a sacred place, such as a shrine, protected by ecclesiastical immunity. By the use of such places as a haven, by extension the term has come to be used for any place of safety. This secondary use can be categorized into human sanctuary, a safe place for people, such as a political sanctuary; and non-human sanctuary, such as an animal or plant sanctuary."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/StMarysSanctuary.JPG/330px-StMarysSanctuary.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanctuary","wikidata":"Q29553"},{"title":"Sanctuary (Canadian TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Sanctuary is a Canadian science fantasy television series created by Damian Kindler. It aired on Syfy in the United States between 2008 and 2011, for all four seasons and a total of 59 episodes. The series also aired in Canada on The Movie Network and Movie Central for the first season, and on Space for seasons 2–4."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/04/Sanctuary_2008_intertitle.png/330px-Sanctuary_2008_intertitle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanctuary_(Canadian_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q844099"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Aias_Kassandra_Louvre_G458.jpg/500px-Aias_Kassandra_Louvre_G458.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Aias_Kassandra_Louvre_G458.jpg/1280px-Aias_Kassandra_Louvre